# Security-GATE configuration files: changes here auto-request review from the
# security owner (visibility, not blocking - require_code_owner_review is
# deliberately OFF, and this repository has no ruleset requiring review at all
# yet; GitHub does not count a PR author's own approval, so a sole owner would
# deadlock their own security PRs).
#
# This file is also what makes `approved-by` in .circleci/security-waivers.yaml
# mean something: validate-waivers requires every approver to appear here.
#
# Deliberately NOT owned: the base-image Dockerfiles and the chart template. The
# gates guard those (misconfig-scan catches hardening regressions, the image
# gates catch package regressions), and owning them would route every dependency
# bump here as noise.
/.circleci/          @MarkusReadius
/.github/            @MarkusReadius
/.trivyignore*       @MarkusReadius
# The trivy secret-scanner config lives under /.circleci/ (owned above); this
# pattern catches a copy landing at the repo root, which is where the orb's own
# default parameter value points.
/trivy-secret.yaml   @MarkusReadius
# Posture scorecard: a security record.
/.security/          @MarkusReadius
# Scan-scope control files: shrinking SAST scope (.semgrepignore) or un-ignoring
# a path (.gitignore) must surface to the security owner.
/.semgrepignore      @MarkusReadius
/.gitignore          @MarkusReadius
/SECURITY.md         @MarkusReadius
